Please extract the 2010 research expenditure data for health-related institutions into JSON using the provided schema, capturing each institution’s breakdown across categories like R&D expenditures, indirect costs, capital outlays, research foundation expenditures, pass-throughs from the Texas Engineering Experiment Station, and total research expenditures as determined by the research survey.

=== Report ===
The research expenditures of health-related institutions, as summarized for fiscal year 2010, reveal a detailed breakdown of costs and funding streams reported as of December 21, 2011. The tabular summary captures several expense categories, contributing to a nuanced understanding of institutional financial commitments to research. Among the columns are total research expenditures measured per SRECNA, delineation of R&D spending that does not meet the definition used in the official research expenditure survey, and indirect costs linked to research and development activities. Additional line items include capital outlays for research infrastructure, institutional research foundation expenditures, pass-through amounts from the Texas Engineering Experiment Station, and the calculated total of research expenditures as determined by the standardized survey methodology.

This structure enables the analysis of not only headline spending totals but also the composition and routing of funds within and across health-related academic institutions. The presence of separate categories for “Indirect Costs Associated w/ R&D” and pass-through funds reflects attention to the full economic footprint of research activity, while the capital outlay column speaks to institutional investment in long-term research capacity. Furthermore, by distinguishing between R&D that qualifies under standard definitions and expenditures falling short of those criteria, the data permit a sharper assessment of formal compliance and possible variability in reporting approaches.

A review of the financial allocation and cost architecture can be gleaned from ## Sheet: Sheet1

| Unnamed: 0   | Unnamed: 1                       | Unnamed: 2                                                   | Health-Related Institutions              | Unnamed: 4                  | Unnamed: 5                                               | Unnamed: 6                               | Return to Index                                               |
|:-------------|:---------------------------------|:-------------------------------------------------------------|:-----------------------------------------|:----------------------------|:---------------------------------------------------------|:-----------------------------------------|:--------------------------------------------------------------|
| nan          | nan                              | nan                                                          | FY 2010 Summary of Research Expenditures | nan                         | nan                                                      | nan                                      | nan                                                           |
| nan          | nan                              | nan                                                          | December 21, 2011                        | nan                         | nan                                                      | nan                                      | nan                                                           |
| Institution  | Research Expenditures Per SRECNA | R & D Not Meeting the Definition of the Research Exp. Survey | Indirect Costs Associated w/ R & D       | Capital Outlay for Research | Institution's Research Foundation Expenditures for R & D | Pass Throughts From TX Eng. Exp. Station | Total Research Expenditures As Deetermined by Research Survey |
| Total        | nan                              | nan                                                          | nan                                      | nan                         | nan                                                      | nan                                      | nan                                                           |
| nan          | nan                              | nan                                                          | nan                                      | nan                         | nan                                                      | nan                                      | Amounts for Formula Funding                                   |
, which encapsulates these expense dimensions in a single, comparative view. This consolidated format not only aids stakeholders in auditing the effective deployment of resources but also serves as a benchmark for evaluating whether formula funding amounts are appropriately calibrated in light of actual expenditure patterns.

Taken together, the reported figures invite further scrutiny into the relationships among direct expenditures, institutional supports, external pass-throughs, and regulatory definitions. These insights are essential for understanding the drivers of research productivity, ensuring transparency in public investment, and formulating strategies that align spending with institutional research missions.

