The mechanism unfolds as follows: employers first classify the new hire into an eligible target category, such as veterans or various other federally recognized groups. Once the classification is determined, employers are prompted to project both the hourly wage and the anticipated hours worked in the first year. The calculation of potential tax credits is contingent upon these projections and group-specific requirements.

