The material composition and component allocation across console types reveal distinct patterns tailored to varying complexity and user needs. Among the core elements common to both simple and advanced configurations are items such as the reading rack assembly and owner’s manual, which maintain consistent presence but differ subtly in part identification and application.

Specifically, the reading rack assembly is indicated twice with minor variations aligned to the console’s sophistication: the simple console uses one variant, while deluxe and premier consoles incorporate a closely related alternative, suggesting design refinements that accompany feature enhancements. This is further supported by the accompanying hardware—screws with different specifications, like length and thread pitch—demonstrating adaptation to the mechanical demands or assembly requirements inherent in more advanced consoles.

