=== Report ===
The analysis explores temporal overlaps between two distinct time frames: a morning-to-midday period (09:00 to 13:00) and a nighttime interval (21:00 to 02:00). The comparison investigates how varying start and end times influence the presence or absence of overlapping segments within these intervals.

Morning schedules initiate as early as 07:00 and extend up to 13:00, while nighttime activities begin around 19:00 and often continue past midnight into early morning hours. Notably, overlaps predominantly occur in segments spanning from 09:00 to roughly 11:00 during the daytime and from 21:00 up to before 02:00 at night, indicating a critical intersection window for these periods.

When schedules start as early as 07:00 and conclude prior to 09:00, no overlap arises between the two ranges. However, as daytime end times approach or exceed 09:00, the first overlaps are registered. For example, intervals from 07:00 to 10:00 or later include overlapping periods from 09:00 onward. Extension of daytime periods beyond 11:00 maintains the overlap until midday.

Nighttime schedules starting at 19:00 and ending closer to midnight or beyond show similar patterns. Overlaps commence once nighttime segments reach or surpass 21:00, coinciding with early morning cutoff times that range between 00:00 and 04:00. Interestingly, when the nighttime schedule terminates earlier, such as at 20:00 or 21:00, overlaps are absent, reflecting temporal disjunction.

Distinct intervals such as from 10:00 to 13:00 continue to show overlapping windows primarily between 10:00 to 11:00, after which overlap disappears, suggesting a narrowing of concurrent activity periods as midday approaches. Conversely, later time windows after 11:00 no longer demonstrate overlaps, underscoring the importance of early morning to late morning time frames for concurrent scheduling.

