At the top of the form, placeholders prompt for fundamental information including the date, time, and venue of the game, as well as team-specific details like gender category, age group, team name, and jersey color. These categories highlight the organized nature of youth soccer events, setting the framework within which the match will occur.

Central to the document is the roster verification section. It segregates players into those eligible to participate in the upcoming game and those who, while part of the overall team roster, are not cleared to play on that date. The form stipulates a maximum of 18 eligible players on the matchday lineup, with additional space allocated for up to four bench personnel. This limitation reflects regulatory standards aimed at fair play and squad management. Furthermore, each player’s identity is recorded by number and name, affording clarity and traceability.

Accountability is built into the structure through certification clauses. The team coach or manager must attest that all listed players are properly registered and meet the governing rules of the National League. Likewise, the requirement for the referee’s signature and printed name, along with the match date, ensures mutual acknowledgment of the official lineup.

