=== Report ===
This report provides an analytical overview of the most recent consolidated balance sheets for two consecutive years—September 30, 2013, and September 30, 2012. It highlights significant fluctuations in key financial categories, examines compositional shifts in assets and liabilities, and offers an interpretation of broad trends in financial structure and solvency.

The balance sheet for 2013 reveals a total asset base of approximately $4.61 billion, compared to $4.29 billion in 2012, representing a moderate increase. Notably, the growth in total assets was primarily driven by a substantial rise in current assets, which grew from $1.26 billion in 2012 to $1.78 billion in 2013. A major contributor to this increase was the significant surge in cash and equivalents, leaping to $713.3 million in 2013 from $206.3 million a year earlier. Investment securities also increased, from a nil balance to $28.8 million, underscoring a possible shift in short-term investment policy. Receivables and inventories remained broadly stable, while restricted cash and investments saw a modest decrease.

Non-current asset categories exhibited more varied movements. Property, plant, and equipment registered a notable decrease, declining from $555.7 million to $483.9 million. Goodwill and other intangibles, another significant component, also decreased, dropping to $1.60 billion in 2013 from $1.66 billion in the preceding year—a potential indication of amortization or impairment activities.

Turning to liabilities, current obligations more than doubled, with total current liabilities swelling to $1.51 billion in 2013 from just $630.3 million in 2012. This striking increase was largely attributable to the introduction of short-term debt, which stood at $826.6 million in 2013 after registering zero in 2012. Accounts payable, jackpot liabilities (current portion), and accrued liabilities also increased, although to a lesser degree. Long-term debt dropped substantially from $1.85 billion to $1.37 billion, suggesting a substantial refinancing or repayment of longer-term obligations, possibly offset by the rise in short-term borrowing.

Shareholders’ equity demonstrated moderate growth, rising to $1.25 billion from $1.20 billion. This upward movement maintains a stable equity buffer despite the shifting debt profile. Total liabilities increased in tandem with total assets, reaching $3.36 billion in 2013 from $3.09 billion in the prior year, thereby sustaining the fundamental balance-sheet equation.

