=== Report ===
This report analyzes the key administrative and compliance requirements mandated by the Indiana Department of Administration for all entities engaged in business with the State of Indiana. The structured sequence of declarations and data requests forms a comprehensive due diligence process, designed to capture both organizational information and specific metrics relevant to state contracting.

The scope of disclosure covers a wide spectrum beginning with fundamental identification details, such as the name and address of the principal firm representative, corporate domicile, and Federal Tax Identification Number. Greater organizational context is gathered through questions about parent or holding companies, including their jurisdictions and addresses, thereby ensuring transparency of ownership structures. The location of the firm’s headquarters further anchors the entity within an operational geography.

Financial and employment metrics represent another critical pillar. The requirements stipulate the reporting of workforce numbers and payroll amounts — both specific to Indiana resident employees and in aggregate across all employees — using the most recently completed IRS W-2 distribution as the benchmark. Additionally, state-specific registrations are substantiated by requesting Indiana Department of Workforce Development and Department of Revenue account numbers. Information pertaining to the dollar value of the active proposal, bid, or contract is also required, promoting fiscal clarity.

A noteworthy feature of these requirements is the granular focus on Indiana residency, especially for labor attached directly to each proposal or contract. The form differentiates between prime contractor and subcontractor, requiring both entities to detail their Full Time Equivalent (FTE) employee counts who are Indiana residents. This targeted inquiry underpins the state’s effort to track and potentially favor contracts with local employment impacts.

