Please extract the event registration data, including participant payment methods, attendance choices, and associated costs, as well as the example participant distribution and total revenue, into JSON following the given schema. Format the information clearly showing the relationship between payment type, attendance option, cost, and participant counts.

=== Report ===
This brief report analyzes participation and payment patterns related to an event with multiple attendance options distributed over two days. The event organizers have structured registration choices clearly around three categories: attending on Tuesday only, Wednesday only, or both days. Each attending choice corresponds to distinct cost values, reflecting the nature and extent of the participation.

The payment methods identified include "Credit Card" and "Cheque," with costs varying according to the selected attendance option. Specifically, participants attending only Tuesday are charged a fee of 40 units, those attending Wednesday are charged 70 units, and those attending both days incur a cost of 110 units. This tiered pricing likely reflects additional services or benefits for multi-day attendance.

No registered participants have been recorded for Day 1 so far, indicating either an early data snapshot or pending registrations for that day. The alignment between payment method and attendance choice suggests the system enables flexible financial transactions catering to the event’s scheduling options.

The following table summarizes the relationships between payment methods, attendance choices, and associated costs, alongside a tally of total registrations for the first day, which currently stands at zero:

## Sheet: Sheet1

| Registration   | Unnamed: 1   | Unnamed: 2           | Unnamed: 3   | Unnamed: 4                 | Unnamed: 5   |
