=== Report ===
An analysis of the quality distribution among different fruit categories reveals notable variations in appearance ratings. Four distinct fruit types—Oranges, Apples, and Bananas—are assessed with classifications of either “Good” or “Bad” appearance. This evaluation provides insights into the consistency of quality within each category, potentially signaling areas for focused quality control or supply chain adjustments.

