Overall, the data reflect the inherent challenges in maintaining consistent quality standards across different fruit categories. The variations observed emphasize the need for targeted quality assurance measures tailored to the unique handling and shelf-life characteristics of each fruit. Such measures might include enhanced monitoring at critical points in the supply chain or stricter criteria for visual grading before retail display.

